Fillets: a rounding whose end piece stops at a crease of one of its faces
ends with the ball turning on about the crease (mitcad#1203).

The case: a rounding along the outline of a bar's end face (a plane)
where a concave arc meets the bar with a small overlap. The bar's
cylinder and the arc's cylinder meet along a line L square to the end
face, at a slight crease, and the bar keeps only a sliver between L and
the end vertex, rounded along its rim. The walk stops at L's section
(the contact on the bar reaches L, the one on the end face lies inside
it), what follows is an extension of no length, and the corner fails
("Corner OnSame : no point on arc").

Now, where the end piece's contact on one face Fs stops at a point P
inside an edge L of Fs that is a line square to the other face, a plane,
at a crease of less than 30 degrees with the face Fk beyond L, and the
end's vertex lies past L (where it is L's own end, as for a rounding
stopped at a crease, the faces beyond L cut the end as before), the ball
turns on about L at P while touching the plane: a horn torus (both radii
the rounding's) about L's line, from L's section until the ball reaches
the plane's edge with the faces it cuts. The stripe ends at L's section
(the pieces past it are dropped) and a corner stripe of that torus closes
the end, in pieces making one face: the turn about P (its side on Fs
degenerated at the apex), then one piece per face the torus meets on its
way to the plane, cut by it (BRepAlgoAPI_Section of the torus's quarter
with the solid; on the design: the bar's sliver, its rim rounding and the
arc's cylinder), all against the plane along the circle about L's foot.
At a first end the corner stripe comes before the stripe and runs from
the plane's edge to the section. A construction of its own beside
PerformPivotAtStepEnd (0951), tried after it in PerformFilletOnVertex.

On the stored design (99ef321f item 22, both ends of the outline) the
result is valid, the boolean differences with the file's body are empty
both ways and the new faces match the file's (the pivot torus 0.220835
against 0.220833 mm^2). Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_corners.cpp, a
bar with a concave arc meeting it with a small overlap and its rim
rounded, the end face's outline rounded (no result without the patch).
